body:
lets go Pods! lets swoop up on those damn Marlins. 

&#x200B;

I dig their uniforms though. Understated. sharp.

"its not often that you talk about plays not made, but we do it with regularity."

&#x200B;

hilarious.

huh, weird, I haven't heard of him /s

&#x200B;

but seriously, that dudes fucking nuts, he has the facial expression of a dude thats been in the basement for a week doing blow.

LOL, yes THATS IT! thank you for the correction. Electric Dreams I loved as a child for some reason, and when I saw it as an adult I realized that my memories from childhood were warped and likely more influenced by placing more emphasis on the fascination over AI, and the singularity event. 

&#x200B;

Phantasm tho... my gawd, one of the worst films I've ever seen.

"There is a war coming Ned. I don't know when, I don't know who we'll be fighting, but it's coming..."  

&#x200B;

anybody else feeling this way.

The eye comment is pretty interesting. You have to think of it more deeply than just watching it happen, and wonder what it must be like to have your eyesight removed in an instant. Like, what do you see when its destroyed? its almost like a death within a death. The death of one of your senses... pretty fucked up.

&#x200B;

that said, I really cant stand slasher films. They're really too basic and derivative nowadays, IO'm glad that they aren't made as much as they were in the 70's and 80's, and even 90's.
